UID:f99773d1f3b7960d7227fb4a34c50cc09142026_1:43:25_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:MCC Monday
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://catsoncampus.northwestern.edu/rsvp?id=376563
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a Block Printing Workshop. We will spend time together to learn the basics of linoleum block printing– including designing, carving, and printing original prints. All skill levels are welcome and all materials will be provided for use in session. We hope this space will be one of collective artmaking, communal healing, and visioning of better worlds!\n\nTabitha Wiggins, Assistant Vice President for Campus Inclusion and Community, will join us for this special edition of MCC Mondays. Come create with Yasmeen, MSA staff, and Tabitha.\n\nSpace is limited. RSVP on ‘Cats on Campus.\n\nBios:\nYasmeen Khayr (she/her) is a Muslim, Lebanese artist, community-based researcher and facilitator, and art therapist-in-training, based in Rogers Park. She loves artmaking as a release of creative energy and emotional expression. Yasmeen is inspired by the power of communal artmaking as a practice of radical imagining and building of new worlds. Yasmeen plays with linoleum block printing, embroidery, painting, and mixed media creations.\n\nTabitha (she/they) is the Assistant Vice President for Campus Inclusion and Community. They grew up on the south side of Chicago. They returned home to Chicago in 2024 to work with the NU community to create a place where students, staff, and faculty of all backgrounds could not only survive but thrive. They are passionate about student success, Black futures, and living alongside their dog, Denver. \n---\nEvent Details: https://catsoncampus.northwestern.edu/rsvp?id=376563
END:VEVENT
